## Infrastructure Flaws and Issues

1. **SSL Termination at the Load Balancer Level**:
   When SSL terminates at the load balancer, the data packets move from HAProxy to the backend application servers over unencrypted HTTP through the private network layer. If an internal network intrusion happens, an attacker can sniff unencrypted traffic between internal machines.

2. **Only One MySQL Server Capable of Accepting Writes**:
   While the Primary-Replica cluster scales reads, having only one Primary write instance means the platform possesses a severe write-path bottleneck. If the Primary database node undergoes a hard freeze, the application can no longer update user profiles, handle checkouts, or execute database writes.

3. **Servers with All the Same Components (Database, Web Server, App Server)**:
   Running Nginx, the Application Server, and MySQL concurrently on every single node introduces resource contention. A massive SQL lookup query can consume 100% CPU and starve Nginx of resource cycles, causing the web layers to crash due to database system spikes. It is architecturally preferred to split these layers into separate dedicated instances.
